                <pb facs="0855" n="769" sameAs="frus:frus1903/pg769"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Leishman to Mr.
                            Hay.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Constantinople</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1903-08-27"><hi rendition="#italic">August 27,
                        1903</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>(Mr. Leishman reports that he has just received a telegram from the United States
                    consul at Beirut advising that the vice-consul was assassinated the preceding
                    Sunday night while driving in a carriage; that the murderer was unseen and
                    unknown; no explanation given for delay in reporting the case, but the consul
                    adds that the reply of the local governor is unsatisfactory.</p>
                <p>Mr. Leishman has asked for further particulars, and will at once make vigorous
                    representations at the Sublime Porte.)</p>
            </div>
